# Keep Docker build contexts small and reproducible. Every service image is
# built from the repo root (monorepo workspaces), so this one file guards all
# of them. Never ship local state, secrets, installed deps, or build output —
# `npm ci` reinstalls from the lockfile inside the image.

# Installed dependencies (reinstalled deterministically from package-lock.json)
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Local databases and their journals (each container gets a fresh volume)
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal

# Secrets and local env — must be injected at runtime, never baked in
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Frontend build output (regenerated by `vite build` in the image)
**/dist

# Test, coverage, and CI artifacts — not needed at runtime
test-results
playwright-report
coverage
**/*.log

# VCS and tooling metadata
.git
.github
.husky
.vscode
.idea

# Docs and specs are not needed inside runtime images (migrations are *.sql,
# so they are unaffected by these markdown/dir excludes and ship with the API).
docs
openspec
**/*.md

# The Dockerfiles themselves and compose files
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
